Task: React adapter keyboard and ARIA (part of Phase 3)
Scope: packages/core/src/{accessibility.ts,index.ts}, packages/react/src/{Heelslide.tsx,useHeelslide.ts,types.ts}, + 2 new test files

TDD: Red (12 failing of 22) -> Green (62 package specs passing).
tsc -b clean, oxlint clean.

Design decision: the key map moved into core (resolveKeyAction, KEY_SHORTCUTS,
KeyAction) rather than being written per adapter. Parity across three adapters
is then structural rather than maintained by hand, and the deliberate omission
of End - which would let one keypress bypass path traversal - is enforced once.
Also covers 'Spacebar', the legacy key name some assistive technology still
reports.

Local-only snag worth recording: adapters resolve core's types from dist, so a
stale dist produced spurious errors in packages/svelte. Rebuilding core cleared
it. Not a CI issue - tsconfig project references make tsc -b build core's
declarations first, and CI starts from a clean checkout.

Remaining in Phase 3: slider normalization for Vue and Svelte (their role sits
on an SVG <g>), the visible focus indicator, and the two adapters' keyboard and
ARIA work.
